# Copy to .env.local when you need to override the default.
#
# Unset is fine for both normal cases:
#   npm run dev        -> BASE is /api and vite.config.js proxies it to localhost:8000
#   Capacitor build    -> BASE is http://localhost:8000/api, reached over `adb reverse`
#
# Set it when the API is anywhere else — a LAN box, a staging host, a tunnel. Include the
# /api suffix; api/client.js appends paths directly to whatever is here.
#
# VITE_API_BASE=https://kaarigar-staging.example.in/api
#
# Untethered phone — no USB cable, no `adb reverse`, phone and laptop on the same WiFi.
# Use the laptop's own LAN address (`ip -4 -o addr show scope global`), and serve the API
# on 0.0.0.0 so it is not bound to loopback:
#
#   VITE_API_BASE=http://192.168.1.23:8000/api
#
# Cleartext to a LAN address is permitted in DEBUG builds only, by
# android/app/src/debug/res/xml/network_security_config.xml. `assembleRelease` is still
# loopback-only, so this cannot follow the app into the field.
